  "visualBrief": "Specific standing Romulus exterior: round weathered brick/lime body, concentric shallow tiled roof rings, eight-sided arched-window lantern and gray metal dome; projecting pale portal with purple shafts/leafy capitals and static closed green bronze paired leaves/panels/studs. Concave lower entrance wings with recessed arched niches, two standing right-hand columns and broken left bases. Neighboring church and independent halls remain native. No hidden ritual interior, copied sculpture/text atlas or complete restoration of missing front colonnades.",
